maya (DevEx): Heads-up — got a support ticket where the edge sample app breaks when people copy the Node CJS snippets. Error: "TypeError: Cannot read property 'default' of undefined" in Workers. Also they said 401s keep getting retried and it loops. Can we clarify docs + samples?

samir (SDK): Yup, two separate issues. 1) Edge runtimes are ESM-first (Cloudflare/Deno/ServiceWorkers). If a sample shows `const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference')` users will hit interop problems depending on bundler. 2) Retry behavior — 401 should not be retried by default.

andre (Runtime): Quick note: Cloudflare Workers and some edge envs don't support Node timers the same way, so our SDK fallback retry logic that uses setTimeout can behave weirdly when polyfilled. For auth failures we explicitly shouldn't retry.

maya (DevEx): Example repro I got from user (they pasted):
```js
// they used this in a worker file
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: MY_KEY });
await client.generate('hello');
// -> TypeError: Redwood.default is not a constructor
```

samir (SDK): That's the classic CJS/ESM interop. Two safe patterns to put in docs: ESM-first (preferred for edge):
```js
// ESM (recommended for Cloudflare, Deno, Vercel Edge)
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
await client.generate('hi');
```
Or for consumers stuck on CommonJS (Node, old scripts):
```js
// CommonJS (Node only)
const mod = require('@redwood/inference');
const RedwoodClient = mod?.default ?? mod?.RedwoodClient ?? mod;
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
```
Add a comment about `esModuleInterop: true` in tsconfig for TS folks so `import Redwood from '...'` behaves.

alice (edge-ci): Also call out bundlers: Vite/ESBuild sometimes preserve ESM and you must set `build.target` appropriately. We should add a tiny Vite snippet for ESM output and a note about using `define: { 'process.env.NODE_ENV': '"production"' }` to avoid accidental polyfills that change module shape.

maya (DevEx): Good. For the 401/retry part — user said they saw repeated 401 then infinite retries and eventual rate limit. We need a clear doc sentence: 401 = do not retry by default; other 5xx/429 should use backoff (but avoid unbounded retries).

samir (SDK): Agreed. SDK change we already discussed in PR: default retry policy will not retry on 401 and caps total attempts (maxRetries: 3) with jittered exponential backoff. For edge runtimes we fall back to synchronous retries (no long timers) so we also lower attempt count there. I'll link the PR in a sec.

andre (Runtime): For reproducibility in docs, include a short troubleshooting checklist:
- Confirm runtime (Cloudflare / Deno / Node)
- Use ESM import for edge runtimes
- Show CJS fallback pattern for Node only
- Check tsconfig `esModuleInterop` if types mismatch
- If auth error, confirm token source and expiration, do not enable auto-retry for 401

docs-bot: Noted. Creating a docs issue with labels: docs, devex, edge-sdk, auth-retry. Will attach sample snippets + tsconfig examples and a Vite section.

maya (DevEx): One more UX nit — sample app quickstarts currently have a mix: some folders use `require`, some `import`. We should standardize quickstarts per runtime folder (node/, worker/, vite/). I'll open a microtask to sweep examples.

samir (SDK): I'll update README examples to show ESM first, then a CJS appendix. Also will add a short note about named vs default exports and the `mod?.default ?? mod` pattern.

maya (DevEx): Great. For the doc content: can we include this tiny tsconfig snippet?
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "ESNext",
    "target": "ES2020",
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "moduleResolution": "Node"
  }
}
```
And a Vite note: `build.lib.formats: ['es']` for edge deployments.

alice (edge-ci): I'll run the sample smoke tests after changes. If anyone wants to add more failing repros, drop them here and I'll queue.

maya (DevEx): Awesome — assigning action items: samir update SDK README + samples, docs-bot open issue, alice run CI checks. Thanks. :pray:
